#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0640 expect=violation domain=ADAE
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when SDTM SUPPAE contains a record with QNAM=AETRTEM for a subject but AETRTEM is not a column of the corresponding ADVERSE EVENT sub-class OCCDS (ADaM) dataset.
#note "Written FIRST in runbook W2a (PLAN-operation-replacements phase 0), on the pre-change engine: the pivot this rule exists for (Fix #39) had no scenario. AETRTEM is NOT a literal AE column; it is delivered ONLY as a SUPPAE QNAM. The qualified requirement AE.AETRTEM is met through the SUPP pivot (OperatorRegistry.existsAsDottedDatasetColumn), ADAE lacks the column -> violation. Under Supp_Merge: true (the default) the pivot answers exactly as before; this scenario is the pin that the default moves nothing here."
#expectViolationCount 1
dataset ADAE
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col ASEQ type=Num
col AETERM type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | 1 | HEADACHE
---

dataset AE label="Adverse Events"
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col AESEQ type=Num
col AETERM type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | 1 | HEADACHE
---

dataset SUPPAE label="Supplemental Qualifiers for AE"
col STUDYID  type=Char
col RDOMAIN  type=Char
col USUBJID  type=Char
col IDVAR    type=Char
col IDVARVAL type=Char
col QNAM     type=Char
col QLABEL   type=Char
col QVAL     type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | AE | 01-701-1015 | AESEQ | 1 | AETRTEM | Treatment Emergent Flag | Y
---
